{"uid":"5b83a6a8e21fc017","name":"test_product_grid_matches_the_visual_baseline[firefox]","fullName":"tests.web.test_accessibility_and_visual#test_product_grid_matches_the_visual_baseline","historyId":"22594ee48703c25802455ad2e9e3b0d4","time":{"start":1786693424715,"stop":1786693426344,"duration":1629},"description":"A hand-rolled visual check, so you can see the mechanics.\n\n    In production use a service (Percy, Applitools, Chromatic) or Playwright's\n    own `expect(page).to_have_screenshot()` in the JS runner. What matters is\n    that you understand the four levers below — every tool exposes the same ones.\n\n    ### A screenshot is only comparable within one environment\n\n    The first CI run of this test failed on all three engines. The baseline had\n    been recorded on Windows/Chromium, and Linux CI renders the same page with\n    different font rasterisation — before you even consider that Firefox and\n    WebKit are different engines entirely.\n\n    That is not a bug to work around, it is the defining property of visual\n    testing: a baseline belongs to one browser on one operating system. Hence\n    the platform- and engine-keyed filename below. In a real project you either\n    commit baselines generated inside the same container CI uses, or you use a\n    hosted service that manages exactly this problem for you.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>A hand-rolled visual check, so you can see the mechanics.</p>\n<pre><code>In production use a service (Percy, Applitools, Chromatic) or Playwright's\nown `expect(page).to_have_screenshot()` in the JS runner. What matters is\nthat you understand the four levers below — every tool exposes the same ones.\n\n### A screenshot is only comparable within one environment\n\nThe first CI run of this test failed on all three engines. The baseline had\nbeen recorded on Windows/Chromium, and Linux CI renders the same page with\ndifferent font rasterisation — before you even consider that Firefox and\nWebKit are different engines entirely.\n\nThat is not a bug to work around, it is the defining property of visual\ntesting: a baseline belongs to one browser on one operating system. Hence\nthe platform- and engine-keyed filename below. In a real project you either\ncommit baselines generated inside the same container CI uses, or you use a\nhosted service that manages exactly this problem for you.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"skipped","statusMessage":"Skipped: No baseline for firefox on linux; recorded one at product-grid.firefox.linux.png. Commit it from the environment CI runs in, then this test starts comparing.","statusTrace":"('/home/runner/work/qa-automation-python/qa-automation-python/tests/web/test_accessibility_and_visual.py', 188, 'Skipped: No baseline for firefox on linux; recorded one at product-grid.firefox.linux.png. Commit it from the environment CI runs in, then this test starts comparing.')","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_session_faker","time":{"start":1786693420379,"stop":1786693420381,"duration":2},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"sut","time":{"start":1786693420381,"stop":1786693420416,"duration":35},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"base_url","time":{"start":1786693420416,"stop":1786693420416,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_verify_url","time":{"start":1786693420416,"stop":1786693420417,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"stepsCount":0,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"attachmentsCou